-- title:
--   Transported level of a Γ-translate equals its χ-twist
-- statement:
--   The setting is the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation package for a fake elliptic curve moduli problem, with the following data and hypotheses.
--
--   **Arithmetic of the base.** Primes $r$ and $\bar r$ with $\bar r \neq r$, and a positive integer $N$ that is squarefree and divisible by neither $r$ nor $\bar r$. A domain $\mathcal O$ of characteristic zero which is a discrete valuation ring, with an irreducible element $\pi$, complete for the $\pi$-adic topology, residue ring of cardinality $r$ and $\mathrm{span}\{r\} = \mathrm{span}\{\pi\}$ (absolute unramifiedness), together with a fraction field $K_0$ of characteristic zero. Over $\mathcal O$, a domain $\mathrm{Onr}$ of characteristic zero with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, complete for the ideal generated by $\pi$, this ideal being maximal; every element of $\mathrm{Onr}$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial of positive degree over $\mathrm{Onr}$ has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^{r}$ modulo $\pi$ (`hFr`), so that $\mathrm{Onr}$ plays the role of the completed unramified extension with its Frobenius lift. A homomorphism $\mathrm{vdet} : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) is given, characterised by `hvdet`: $\mathrm{vdet}(g) = n$ if and only if $\det g$ is a unit of $\mathcal O$ times $\pi^{n}$.
--
--   **Quaternionic data and moduli spaces.** An indefinite quaternion algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ ramified exactly at $r$ and $\bar r$, with a maximal order $\Lambda$; a scheme $\mathcal X$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,\mathcal O$ with a point assignment $\mathrm{pt}$ which is a coarse moduli space for fake elliptic curves of level $N$ (`h𝒳`). An auxiliary level $n \geq 3$ prime to $r$, to $\bar r$ and to $N$; a scheme $M$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,\mathcal O$ with $\mathrm{ptF}$ a fine moduli space for fake elliptic curves with full level $n$ (`hM`); a group $G$ acting on $M$ by $\rho$ with labels $\chi : G \to \Lambda$ satisfying the level-twist axioms (`hρ`); a morphism $p : M \to \mathcal X$ over $\mathcal O$, invariant under $\rho$ and compatible with the two point assignments (`hp`, `hρp`, `hp_pt`). For each prime $\ell$ distinct from $r$ and $\bar r$, a coarse moduli space $\mathcal Y_\ell$ for curves with extra level $\ell$ with its degeneracy maps $d_0,d_1 : \mathcal Y_\ell \to \mathcal X$ over $\mathcal O$, compatible with the point assignments on sources and on $\ell$-isogeny targets (`h𝒴`, `hd₀f`, `hd₁f`, `hd₀`, `hd₁`); Atkin–Lehner endomorphisms $a_r, a_{\bar r}$ of $\mathcal X$ over $\mathcal O$ realising the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and at $\bar r$ on points (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **The definite side.** A definite quaternion algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ ramified exactly at $\bar r$, a maximal order $\Lambda_1$, an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ contained in $\Lambda_1$, an element $n_1$ of the $r$-th prime Hecke set of $R_1$ such that the intersection order $R_1 \cap n_1 R_1 n_1^{-1}$ is Eichler of level $Nr$, an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra embedding $\iota_0$ into $M_2(K_0)$, and a place $v$ of $\mathbb Q$ above $r$. The group $\Gamma_t$ is the group of units of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ integral away from $v$ for $R_1$ (`hΓt`). Families $s_\ell$ of units and $s^{f}_\ell$ of finite-adelic units indexed by the primes $\ell \neq r,\bar r$ are given, subject to `hs`: at every finite place not above $r$ the local component of $s^f_\ell$ is $s_\ell \otimes 1$; at the places above $r$ it is $1$; the diagonal image of the scalar $\ell$ times $(s^f_\ell)^{-1}$ lies in the level Hecke set of $\Lambda_1$ and $R_1 \cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ at $\ell$ when $\ell \mid N$, and in the prime Hecke set of that order at $\ell$ otherwise; and the reduced norm of $s_\ell$ is $\ell$. The groups $\Gamma_{t,\ell}$ are defined to be $\Gamma_t$ intersected with its conjugate by $s_\ell$ (`hΓtℓ`). An element $\bar w$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma_t$ is given (`hwbar`). Furthermore $\mathbb Z \subseteq \Lambda$ (`hΛℤ`) and $\mathrm{coord}$ is a system of order coordinates for $\Lambda$ at $r$ (`hcoord`).
--
--   **The curve over the residue ring and its Γ-action.** A fake elliptic curve $A_0$ over $\mathrm{Onr}/\pi$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$ over the same ring, formal coordinates $\theta_0$ of length $2$ for $A_0$ making $A_0$ a formal module via $\mathrm{coord}$, $X_0$ and $\theta_0$ (`hX₀`, `hA₀`); families $e, e'$ of endomorphisms of $A_0$ indexed by $\Gamma_t$ with $e\gamma$ over the base, and degrees $\mathrm{deg}$. The hypotheses `hE1`, `hE1mul`, `hE1sc`, `hE1'`, `hE2`, `hE3`, `hE4` (summarised here) state respectively: each pair $(e\gamma, e'\gamma)$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ preserving the $N$-level; multiplicativity of $\gamma \mapsto e\gamma$ up to powers of $r$; that scalars $c \in \mathbb Z$ in $\Gamma_t$ act, up to powers of $r$, as $A_0$-multiplication by $c$, and conversely that only scalars act this way; that for any injective embedding of the centraliser of the $X_0$-action and of $\varpi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ there is $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ such that every $\gamma$ is realised on formal coordinates by an element of that centraliser whose image is $r^{k_\gamma} g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$; that the action of $\Gamma_t$ on the full level $n$ structure $P_0$ is given by labels $\mathrm{lab}$ in $\Lambda$, multiplicative and compatible with scalars modulo $n$; and that over any algebraically closed extension every $r$-power-degree level-preserving isogeny of a pullback of $A_0$ comes, up to powers of $r$, from some $e\gamma$. A suborder $R_2 \leq R_1$ with $r$-power denominators (`hR₂`, `hR₂o`, `hR₂r`) is given together with endomorphisms $\hat e$ of $A_0$ indexed by $R_2$ over the base, subject to `hE5a`–`hE5e` (summarised here): each $\hat e x$ is additive, commutes with the $\Lambda$-action and preserves the level; $\hat e$ is unital, multiplicative and agrees with integral multiplication; $\hat e(\bar x)\hat e(x)$ is multiplication by the reduced norm; $\hat e$ is compatible with $e$ on elements of the form $r^{k}\gamma$; and a joint matrix realisation of the $\Gamma_t$- and $R_2$-actions with a single conjugating $g$.
--
--   **The Drinfeld moduli package.** A ring homomorphism $\iota$ from the Witt ring $\mathbb Z_{r^2}$ to $\mathrm{Onr}$; a special formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ of height $4$ over $\mathrm{Onr}/r$; a moduli package $\mathrm{MD}$ over $\mathrm{Onr}$ which is a Zariski sheaf, with a classifying map $\eta$ from rigidified objects, satisfying `hη`: $\eta$ separates admissible rigidified objects exactly up to isomorphism, is natural in the base, and is locally surjective on a Zariski cover. An injective embedding $E_0$ of the centraliser of $\Phi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ whose image is commensurable to $M_2(\mathcal O)$ with a uniform $r$-power denominator (`hE₀`). The natural transformation $eD$ identifies the functor of points of $\mathrm{MD}$ over $\mathcal O$ with the product of the functor of $\mathrm{Onr}$-algebra maps and Drinfeld's functor $\Omega$ of Deligne data: `hnatD` (naturality), `hbijD` (bijectivity), `hfstD` (first component is the structure map), `hGLD` (the $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$-action on $\mathrm{MD}$-points corresponds to the twisted action on $\Omega$-points through $\mathrm{vdet}$), `hPiD` and `hPiexD` (the $\pi$-translation corresponds to a single Frobenius twist of the first component, and always exists).
--
--   **Comparison of the two reductions.** Ring maps $\kappa$ and the compatibility `hκ` relating $\mathrm{Onr}/\pi$ and $\mathrm{Onr}/r$, and an isogeny $\beta_0$ of height $4n_0$ from $\Phi$ to the reduction of $X_0$ along $\kappa$. A full level $n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$. The Atkin–Lehner data at $\bar r$ over the residue ring: a curve $A_{0w}$, maps $a_w, a_w', b_w, b_w'$ with $a_w, a_w'$ exhibiting $A_{0w}$ as the $\bar r$-Atkin–Lehner quotient of $A_0$ (`hALw`), $(b_w,b_w')$ an isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_w}$ preserving the level (`hBSw`, `hBSwlev`), and `hJOINTw`, asserting a joint matrix realisation, with one conjugator $g$, of all $\gamma \in \Gamma_t$ and of the composite $a_w$ followed by $b_w$, the latter corresponding to $\iota_0(\bar w)$ up to a power of $r$.
--
--   **The classifying map on rigidified curves.** A map $\Xi$ sending a rigidified fake elliptic curve over a Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent to a point of $\mathrm{MD}$ over $B$, subject to: `hΞleg` (over a connected base the structure map of $\Xi$ is a Frobenius twist of the given one), `hΞnat` (naturality along pullbacks of rigidified curves), `hΞiso` ($\Xi$ identifies rigidified curves related by an isomorphism together with a comparison of their rigidifications up to powers of $r$), and `hΞdef` (on a connected base with $r$ nilpotent, $\Xi$ is computed by transporting the formal module structure through $\theta_0$, $\kappa$, $\beta_0$ to an admissible rigidified object $t$ with shift $j \leq 1$, and $\Xi$ equals the class of $\eta(t)$ at the $(-j)$-fold Frobenius twist). A matrix $g_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ is fixed, and `heqΓ`, `heqW` assert that $\Gamma_t$-translates of rigidifications, respectively the $\bar r$-Atkin–Lehner correspondence matched with $a_w$ followed by $b_w$, are carried by $\Xi$ to the $\mathrm{MD}$-action of $r^{c} g_0 \iota_0(\gamma) g_0^{-1}$, respectively $r^{c} g_0 \iota_0(\bar w) g_0^{-1}$, for some integer $c$. The hypotheses `hK1`–`hK4` state, for the correspondence between rigidified curves over $B$ and $\Omega$-points twisted by $g_0^{-1}$: existence (`hK1`), uniqueness up to isomorphism with a comparison of rigidifications (`hK2`), pullback along $\mathcal O$-algebra maps (`hK3`), and a lifting property along surjections with square-zero kernel-type hypothesis, together with the invariance of the twisted-action condition under the replacement of the rigidification (`hK4`). The hypotheses `hC0e` and `hC0u` give, over a connected base with a formal module structure, existence and uniqueness of a full level $n$ structure which is a height-normalised transport of $P_0$ along a rigidification, in the sense of `IsNormLevelTransport`.
--
--   **The family over the fine moduli space.** A natural transformation $\Theta_f$ from the product of the $\mathrm{Onr}$-points functor, $\Omega$ and the constant functor $G$ to the functor of nilpotent points of $f_M$, natural in the base (`hnat`), with $G$ acting on the third factor through $\rho$ (`hG`), and matching $\mathrm{ptF}$ at $g = 1$ on curves with their transported level (`hC2`), hence matching $\mathrm{pt}$ after composition with $p$ (`hC2c`).
--
--   **The level-homomorphism law.** An injective embedding $EX$ of the centraliser of $X_0$; an integer $N_\beta$ and a series $\beta_0'$ which is an $\mathcal O_D$-homomorphism from the reduction of $X_0$ to $\Phi$ quasi-inverse to $\beta_0$ up to $r^{N_\beta}$ (`hβ₀'`, `hβ₀'β₀`, `hβ₀β₀'`), and `hEXE₀` comparing $EX$ with $E_0$ through $\beta_0,\beta_0'$ with factor $r^{N_\beta}$. A conjugator $g_X$, elements $\varepsilon_\gamma$ of the centraliser and integers $k_\gamma$ realising each $\gamma$ on the formal coordinates of $A_0$ through $e\gamma$ and satisfying $EX(\varepsilon_\gamma) = r^{k_\gamma} g_X \iota_0(\gamma) g_X^{-1}$ (`hεk`). A homomorphism $\mathrm{slack} : \Gamma_t \to (\mathbb Z/n)^\times$ with $\mathrm{slack}(\gamma)\, r^{(-k_\gamma)^{+}} = r^{k_\gamma^{+}}$ in $\mathbb Z/n$ (`hslack`), and a homomorphism $\theta_t : \Gamma_t \to G$ such that for every $\gamma$ the point $P_0$ pushed by $e\gamma$ and then by the action of $\chi(\theta_t\gamma)$ equals $P_0$ pushed by multiplication by the representative of $\mathrm{slack}(\gamma)$ (`hθt`). Finally `hC3` asserts, for a connected base with the above matching data, that a twisted action of $\iota_0(\gamma)$ on $(\psi,P)$ is realised by another rigidification $\varrho'$ of the same curve, whose transported level differs from the original one by the action of $\chi(\theta_t\gamma)$, and that the extra level structures at primes $\ell \neq r$ invertible on the base are unchanged.
--
--   **The situation considered.** Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra with $\pi$ nilpotent, $\psi : \mathrm{Onr} \to k$ an $\mathcal O$-algebra map, and $P, P'$ two Deligne data over $k$. Write $\psi_0$ for the Frobenius twist of $\psi$ by $-\mathrm{vdet}(g_0)$. Let $E$ with rigidification $\varrho$ and $E'$ with rigidification $\varrho'$ be fake elliptic curves over $k$ relative to $\psi_0$, such that the structure map of $\Xi$ on each is $\psi_0$ and the corresponding $\Omega$-point, twisted by $g_0^{-1}$, is $(\psi,P)$ respectively $(\psi,P')$ (`hΞψ`, `hev`, `hΞψ'`, `hev'`). Let $i : E.A \cong E'.A$ be an isomorphism over $k$ compatible with the group laws, the $\Lambda$-action and the $N$-level structures (`hi`, `hvia`). Let $\gamma \in \Gamma_t$, and let $\varrho''$ be a further rigidification of $E$ relative to $\psi_0$ whose $\Xi$-image has structure map $\psi_0$ and twisted $\Omega$-point $(\psi,P')$ (`hev''`), where $(\psi,P)$ and $(\psi,P')$ are related by the twisted action of $\iota_0(\gamma)$ (`htw`), $\varrho''$ is the $e\gamma$-translate of $\varrho$ (`htr`), and $\varrho''$ corresponds to $\varrho'$ along $i$ in the sense of `hcorr`: there are a morphism $ib$ of the special fibres with $ib$ followed by $\varrho'.gb$ equal to $\varrho''.gb$ followed by $i$, compatible with the structure morphisms, a pullback comparison $uA$ of the auxiliary curves with $uA$ followed by $\varrho''.gA$ equal to $\varrho'.gA$, and natural numbers $i_1, j_1$ such that $ib$ followed by $\varrho'.\varphi$, $uA$ and multiplication by $r^{i_1}$ coincides with $\varrho''.\varphi$ followed by multiplication by $r^{j_1}$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every full level $n$ structure $P_n$ on $E$ and every full level $n$ structure $P_n'$ on $E'$, if $P_n$ is a height-normalised transport of $P_0$ along $\varrho$ and $P_n'$ is a height-normalised transport of $P_0$ along $\varrho'$ (both in the sense of `IsNormLevelTransport` for the data $\mathrm{Fr}, \theta_0, \kappa, \beta_0, \Phi, \iota, \mathrm{coord}, P_0$), then the point $P_n.P$ pushed forward by the action of $\chi(\theta_t\gamma)$ on $E$ and then transported along $i$ equals $P_n'.P$; that is, $P_n.P$ composed with $E.\mathrm{act}(\chi(\theta_t\gamma))$ and then with $i$ is $P_n'.P$ as a section of $E'$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,k$.
--
--   This is the level-structure half of the one-leg fibre computation in the Čerednik–Drinfeld description of the special fibre of a Shimura curve: it says that passing from a rigidification to its $\Gamma_t$-translate moves the height-normalised transported full level $n$ structure exactly by the label $\chi(\theta_t\gamma)$, compatibly with the isomorphism of the underlying fake elliptic curves. It is used in the assembly of the one-leg fibre of the fine family, where the resulting points of the fine moduli space are identified up to the twisting action of $G$.
